**3:3** The deposit therefore has silted over in you; something was once placed into open hands and unstopped ears; and a thing not held leaks out of the holder, and your mind is facing the wrong wall; if therefore you do not know that you are unconscious, ⸀arrival is indistinguishable from loss, and the ⸀clock you carry has no numbers on it upon you;

**3:4** But against the total saturation, ⸂there persists within your jurisdiction, despite everything, a countable⸃ number of names inside the saturated zone who did not know the dye through which they moved marking them without being noticed, and they are legible to the speaker; contact is restored in the visible fact of non-absorption, for their surface still corresponds to what was transmitted.

**3:5** Whoever has remained porous to the original signal and opaque to the ambient saturation ⸀on exactly these terms will be wrapped in the evidence of having refused the local dye, and in the register where being-recognized and being-alive are the same entry the inscription will not be dissolved — non-erasure is an act — and his name I will pronounce so as to cause to exist before witnesses, before the source of the authority that authorizes the speaker and before the field of operational attention that surrounds the source.
